  "description": "AHAFUL crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C16 H68 Dy6 N16 O23 8+,8(Cl1 1-),2(C4 H8 N4),6(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.455-5.212 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.19-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy6(μ6-O)(μ3-OH)8(L)4(H2O)14]Cl8·2L·6H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ6-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 14 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ6-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 14 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
